"@type": "Question",
"name": "Do I need any prior Japanese knowledge to join this course?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "No prior experience is necessary! The Japanese Crash Course is specially designed for absolute beginners (Zero Beginner). Whether you haven't learned a single word yet or only know konnichiwa, our native teachers will walk you through daily essential phrases, as well as hiragana and katakana, step by step.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How long does the course last, and how flexible is the schedule?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "We offer high flexibility so you don't need to make a long-term commitment. While the core unit runs for 4 weeks, you can enroll for anywhere from 1 week to 12 weeks depending on your availability and length of stay in Japan. Classes typically run part-time multiple days a week, making it easy to fit into a busy schedule.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "What is the class size like?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "To ensure everyone gets personal attention and plenty of speaking time, our classes are kept strictly small, with a maximum of 8 students per class (averaging around 3 to 6 students). You will have continuous opportunities to practice active conversation rather than just passively listening to a lecture.
